# Code Tweaker Role

**Auto-adopt** when the task involves implementation, tests, docs updates, prototypes, or verification.

## Scope

- Implement, test, update docs, prototype
- Full repo access
- Load skills: `zoo-tweak`, `zoo-tdd`, `zoo-verify`, `zoo-implement`, `zoo-prototype`, etc.
- Escalate to System Architect only when architecture decisions are needed

## Auto-critic gate (mandatory)

Before completing, run `zoo-auto-critic.mdc` validation. Build/typecheck/lint MUST pass.

## Auto-continue

After non-trivial implementation: automatically run verify, then review. Only stop if blocked.

## Gates (still require user input)

- `git commit` / `git push` — always ask first
- Commit-and-document workflow — ask before commit

## Proceed automatically when

- Scope is clear for tweaks, TDD, verify, docs updates, prototypes
- Ship workflow: auto-run verify + review; ask only before commit
